      <section class="chapter-section" id="orientation">
        <span class="section-number">00</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Begin with the human bottleneck</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">You ask one agent to inspect the repository. Then you ask it to plan. Then to implement. Then to test. Then you notice a security concern and reprompt it again. The agent appears busy, but you are still classifying every request, changing its role, deciding what context matters, sequencing the phases, and merging the answers. You are the orchestrator.</p>

        <p>That is the failure this lesson targets. The problem is not merely that one agent can make mistakes. It is that a single general-purpose context must repeatedly impersonate product manager, researcher, engineering lead, frontend developer, backend developer, QA engineer, and security reviewer. Each role starts from a diluted purpose. Each handoff travels through you. Your cognitive load grows with every specialist perspective you add.</p>

        <p>The course codebase replaces that manual relay with a multi-team chat system built on the Pi coding-agent harness. The user talks only to one Orchestrator. The Orchestrator classifies the request and delegates to a Planning, Engineering, or Validation lead. Each lead may consult two specialist workers. The workers execute inside explicit file domains. Results move back through the lead, then through the Orchestrator, and arrive as one synthesized answer. The shipped default is <strong>three teams and ten agents</strong>: one Orchestrator, three leads, and six workers.</p>

        <aside class="callout callout--tactic">
          <p class="callout__label">The sentence to carry</p>
          <p><strong>One agent is a ceiling.</strong> Break it with specialized teams behind one interface, then make autonomy safe with explicit roles, persistent expertise, composable skills, and hard domain boundaries.</p>
        </aside>

        <h3>Dan’s six pillars</h3>
        <p>These are not six unrelated features. They form a dependency chain. A chat room without specialized teams is only a prettier single-agent shell. Specialization without memory relearns the domain. Memory without ownership can compound the wrong knowledge. Ownership without enforcement is a suggestion. A hierarchy without configuration becomes hand-wired and hard to scale. Read the chapter with all six in view.</p>

        <div class="pillar-grid" aria-label="Six pillars of the multi-team architecture">
          <article class="pillar-card"><span class="pillar-card__n">1</span><h3>Team leads &amp; workers</h3><p>Depth-2 delegation removes you from the classify, route, and synthesize loop.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar-card"><span class="pillar-card__n">2</span><h3>Expertise &amp; specialization</h3><p>Each role optimizes a narrower purpose than a generic coding agent.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar-card"><span class="pillar-card__n">3</span><h3>Agent memory</h3><p>Per-agent mental models preserve domain knowledge and compound across sessions.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar-card"><span class="pillar-card__n">4</span><h3>Domain ownership</h3><p>Per-path read, upsert, and delete rules bound every agent’s blast radius.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar-card"><span class="pillar-card__n">5</span><h3>Chat room interface</h3><p>You communicate with one Orchestrator while the team coordinates behind it.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar-card"><span class="pillar-card__n">6</span><h3>Config-driven harness</h3><p>The roster lives in YAML; each agent’s deeper anatomy lives in its own Markdown front matter.</p></article>
        </div>

        <h3>What you are training</h3>
        <ul class="learning-objectives">
          <li><strong>Architecture</strong>Recover the user → Orchestrator → lead → worker route and state what each tier may do.</li>
          <li><strong>Safety judgment</strong>Separate prompt-level behavior from structurally enforced file and tool boundaries.</li>
          <li><strong>Fleet design</strong>Place specialization, memory, skills, model tier, and domain rules at the correct configuration layer.</li>
          <li><strong>Operation</strong>Launch, observe, inspect, prune, and domain-test the real course system without inventing a substitute app.</li>
          <li><strong>Evidence</strong>Use the footer, session directory, logs, source files, and blocked tool calls to verify claims about behavior.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="callout callout--warning">
          <p class="callout__label">Source and cost discipline</p>
          <p>The prompt-routing classifier shown in the video is a separate codebase and is not shipped here. The lab runs the multi-team tool against its own source repository, exactly as its README’s local test instructs. Live team runs consume paid model tokens; keep prompts small, record costs, and do not launch the scaled preset casually.</p>
        </div>

        <h3>How to study this chapter</h3>
        <p>Every major idea repeats the same ten moves: hook, picture, frame-backed story, name, worked source example, small practice, fail/fix, current-practice note, retrieval, and teach-back. Do the small practice before revealing the answers. In the lab, collect evidence rather than impressions. “It seemed like a team” is weak. “The lead’s tool call was blocked, a worker ran the read, and the session log records both” is inspectable.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="chapter-section idea-cycle" id="one-interface">
        <span class="section-number">01</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">One interface, many agent experts</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">Adding specialists should increase the system’s capability without increasing the number of conversations you must personally manage.</p>

        <div class="move move--hook">
          <p class="move-label">1 · Hook — concrete failure</p>
          <h3>The operator with nine tabs</h3>
          <p>You open one session for product planning, one for frontend architecture, one for backend work, another for QA, and another for security. Each session needs a different slice of context. A decision from Planning must be copied into Engineering. A test failure must be copied back into implementation. You may have specialists, but you have also created a human message bus.</p>
          <p>This flat arrangement scales the number of interfaces with the number of experts. Every new role adds routing, context transfer, sequencing, and synthesis work to the operator. The system’s intelligence rises while the human’s coordination burden rises with it. The architecture has distributed work but not orchestration.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="move move--picture">
          <p class="move-label">2 · Picture — one narrow waist</p>
          <h3>Keep your cognitive input flat</h3>
          <div class="team-map" role="img" aria-label="A three-tier team with one orchestrator, three leads, and six workers">
            <div class="team-map__tier">
              <span class="team-map__label">Tier 1 · interface</span>
              <div class="team-map__node team-map__node--orch"><b>Orchestrator</b><span>You talk here. It classifies, delegates, tracks, and synthesizes.</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="team-map__tier">
              <span class="team-map__label">Tier 2 · leads</span>
              <div class="team-map__node team-map__node--planning"><b>Planning Lead</b><span>Product direction and scope</span></div>
              <div class="team-map__node team-map__node--engineering"><b>Engineering Lead</b><span>Architecture and implementation route</span></div>
              <div class="team-map__node team-map__node--validation"><b>Validation Lead</b><span>QA and security route</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="team-map__tier">
              <span class="team-map__label">Tier 3 · workers</span>
              <div class="team-map__workers">
                <div class="team-map__node"><b>Product Manager</b><span>Requirements · acceptance</span></div>
                <div class="team-map__node"><b>UX Researcher</b><span>Behavior · journeys</span></div>
                <div class="team-map__node"><b>Frontend Dev</b><span>UI · client state</span></div>
                <div class="team-map__node"><b>Backend Dev</b><span>APIs · data · infra</span></div>
                <div class="team-map__node"><b>QA Engineer</b><span>Tests · regression</span></div>
                <div class="team-map__node"><b>Security Reviewer</b><span>Threats · auth · data</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>The narrow waist is the Orchestrator. The workers can multiply without creating new interfaces for you. The team config describes who exists and when each specialist should be consulted; the Orchestrator absorbs that routing complexity.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="move move--story">
          <p class="move-label">3 · Story — ping the system</p>

--- MA16 CSS A ---
/* MA-2 extends the gold TAC-1 chapter system with team-orchestration diagrams. */
@import url("../vol-1-tac/01-hello-agentic-coding.assets.css");

:root {
  --team-orchestrator: #2f7658;
  --team-planning: #8c6613;
  --team-engineering: #9a3652;
  --team-validation: #9c4f1e;
  --team-worker: #356f9c;
  --team-line: #b9ad9b;
}

.hero--teams::before {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 1.25rem 1.5rem auto auto;
  width: clamp(9rem, 22vw, 18rem);
  height: clamp(9rem, 22vw, 18rem);
  border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 50%;
  background:
    radial-gradient(circle at 50% 20%, var(--team-orchestrator) 0 .38rem, transparent .43rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 20% 52%, var(--team-planning) 0 .32rem, transparent .37rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 50% 52%, var(--team-engineering) 0 .32rem, transparent .37rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 80% 52%, var(--team-validation) 0 .32rem, transparent .37rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 10% 82%, var(--team-worker) 0 .25rem, transparent .3rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 28% 82%, var(--team-worker) 0 .25rem, transparent .3rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 42% 82%, var(--team-worker) 0 .25rem, transparent .3rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 58% 82%, var(--team-worker) 0 .25rem, transparent .3rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 72% 82%, var(--team-worker) 0 .25rem, transparent .3rem),
    radial-gradient(circle at 90% 82%, var(--team-worker) 0 .25rem, transparent .3rem);
  content: "";
  opacity: .42;
}

.hero--teams h1 { max-width: 12ch; }

.hero-system {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, .8fr) auto minmax(12rem, 1fr) auto minmax(14rem, 1.35fr);
  gap: var(--space-3);
  align-items: center;
  padding: var(--space-5);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  background: var(--bg-card);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
}

.hero-system__node {
  display: grid;
  align-content: center;
  min-height: 8rem;
  padding: var(--space-4);
  border: 2px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-inset);
}

.hero-system__node--orchestrator { border-color: var(--team-orchestrator); background: var(--ok-wash); }
.hero-system__node--teams { border-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-wash); }
.hero-system__node b { font: 650 var(--text-md) var(--font-display); }
.hero-system__node span { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }
.hero-system__arrow { color: var(--accent); font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 800; text-align: center; }

.pillar-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-3);
}

.pillar-card {
  min-height: 13rem;
  padding: var(--space-4);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-card);
}

.pillar-card__n {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 2.1rem;
  height: 2.1rem;
  border-radius: 50%;
  color: var(--ink-inverse);
  background: var(--accent);
  font: 750 var(--text-sm) var(--font-mono);
}

.pillar-card h3 { margin-top: var(--space-3); font-size: var(--text-md); }
.pillar-card p { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }

.team-map {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, .72fr) minmax(15rem, 1fr) minmax(22rem, 1.75fr);
  gap: var(--space-4);
  align-items: center;
  padding: var(--space-6);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  background: var(--bg-card);
}

.team-map__tier {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--space-3);
}

.team-map__label {
  color: var(--ink-mute);
  font: 700 var(--text-xs) var(--font-mono);
  letter-spacing: .08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}

.team-map__node {
  padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
  border: 2px solid var(--node-color, var(--border));
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-inset);
}

.team-map__node b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); }
.team-map__node span { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-1); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-xs); }
.team-map__node--orch { --node-color: var(--team-orchestrator); background: var(--ok-wash); }
.team-map__node--planning { --node-color: var(--team-planning); }
.team-map__node--engineering { --node-color: var(--team-engineering); }
.team-map__node--validation { --node-color: var(--team-validation); }
.team-map__workers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-2); }
.team-map__workers .team-map__node { --node-color: var(--team-worker); min-height: 6.5rem; }

.tier-table td:first-child { width: 20%; font-weight: 750; }
.tier-table td:nth-child(2) { width: 18%; }
.tier-table td:last-child { border-left: 3px solid var(--ok); }

.lock-stack {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-4);
  align-items: stretch;
}

.lock-card {
  padding: var(--space-5);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  background: var(--bg-card);
}

.lock-card--hard { border: 2px solid var(--ok); background: var(--ok-wash); }
.lock-card h3 { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
.lock-card p { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--ink-soft); }
.lock-stack__plus { align-self: center; color: var(--accent); font-size: var(--text-xl); font-weight: 800; }

.permission-map {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-3);
}

.permission-map div { padding: var(--space-4); border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg-card); }
.permission-map b { display: block; color: var(--accent-ink); font: 650 var(--text-md) var(--font-display); }
.permission-map span { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }

.memory-loop {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-2);
  align-items: stretch;
}

.memory-loop__step {
  position: relative;
  min-height: 9rem;
  padding: var(--space-4);
  border: var(--hairline);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  background: var(--bg-card);
}

.memory-loop__step:not(:last-child)::after {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  right: calc(var(--space-3) * -1);
  z-index: 2;
  color: var(--accent);
  content: "→";
  font-weight: 800;
}

.memory-loop__step b { display: block; color: var(--accent-ink); font-family: var(--font-display); }
.memory-loop__step span { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-sm); }

.skill-matrix td:first-child { width: 28%; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; }
.skill-matrix .yes { color: var(--ok); font-weight: 800; }
.skill-matrix .no { color: var(--ink-mute); }

.anatomy-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-2);
}

.anatomy-grid div { padding: var(--space-3); border-top: .3rem solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg-card); box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); }
.anatomy-grid b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); }
.anatomy-grid span { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-xs); }

.config-split {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-4);
}

.config-split__card { padding: var(--space-5); border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-card); }
.config-split__card--agent { border-top: .35rem solid var(--team-worker); }
.config-split__card--yaml { border-top: .35rem solid var(--team-planning); }
.config-split__card h3 { margin-top: 0; }
.config-split__card ul { margin-top: var(--space-3); }

.preset-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-2);
}

.preset-grid div { min-height: 8rem; padding: var(--space-3); border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg-card); }
.preset-grid code { display: inline-block; }
.preset-grid span { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-xs); }

.cost-balance {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
  gap: var(--space-4);
  align-items: center;
}

.cost-balance__side { min-height: 12rem; padding: var(--space-5); border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-card); }
.cost-balance__side--value { border: 2px solid var(--ok); background: var(--ok-wash); }
.cost-balance__side h3 { margin-top: 0; }
.cost-balance__side p { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
.cost-balance__mark { color: var(--accent); font: 750 var(--text-2xl) var(--font-display); }

.runtime-flow {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: var(--space-3);
  align-items: stretch;
}

.runtime-flow__node { position: relative; min-height: 10rem; padding: var(--space-4); border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--bg-card); }
.runtime-flow__node:not(:last-child)::after { position: absolute; top: 50%; right: calc(var(--space-4) * -1); z-index: 2; color: var(--accent); content: "→"; font-weight: 800; }
.runtime-flow__node b { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); }
.runtime-flow__node code { display: inline-block; margin-top: var(--space-2); }
.runtime-flow__node span { display: block; margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--text-xs); }

.two-runtimes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-4); }
.two-runtimes article { padding: var(--space-5); border: var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-card); }
.two-runtimes article:first-child { border-top: .35rem solid var(--team-orchestrator); }
.two-runtimes article:last-child { border-top: .35rem solid var(--team-worker); }
.two-runtimes h3 { margin-top: 0; }

.current-links { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-4); }
.current-link { padding: var(--space-5); border: 1px dashed var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--bg-card); }
.current-link h3 { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
.current-link p { margin-top: var(--space-3); color: var(--ink-soft); }

.frame-card img {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: min(100%, 1100px);
  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
  object-fit: contain;
  background: var(--bg-card);
}

.frame-card figcaption { max-width: 78ch; }

.rubric-table th:first-child { width: 18%; }
.rubric-table td:not(:first-child), .rubric-table th:not(:first-child) { text-align: center; }
.rubric-table td:first-child { font-weight: 700; }

.source-note { padding: var(--space-4); border-top: var(--hairline); color: var(--ink-mute); font-size: var(--text-sm); }

@media (max-width: 64rem) {
  .pillar-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .team-map { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .team-map__workers { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .anatomy-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .preset-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .runtime-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .runtime-flow__node:not(:last-child)::after { top: auto; right: 50%; bottom: calc(var(--space-4) * -1); transform: rotate(90deg); }
}

@media (max-width: 48rem) {
  .hero-system,
  .lock-stack,
  .cost-balance { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .hero-system__arrow,
  .lock-stack__plus,
  .cost-balance__mark { transform: rotate(90deg); text-align: center; }
  .pillar-grid,
  .permission-map,
  .config-split,
  .two-runtimes,
  .current-links { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .team-map__workers,
  .anatomy-grid,
  .preset-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .memory-loop { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .memory-loop__step:not(:last-child)::after { top: auto; right: 50%; bottom: calc(var(--space-3) * -1); transform: rotate(90deg); }
}

@media (max-width: 34rem) {
  .team-map__workers,
  .anatomy-grid,
  .preset-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
}

@media print {
  .hero--teams::before { display: none; }
  .pillar-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .pillar-card,
  .team-map__workers .team-map__node,
  .runtime-flow__node { min-height: 0; }
  .source-note { display: none; }
}

