123:      <div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Volume III</p><h2 id="ma-heading">Multi-Agent Systems</h2></div><p>4 of 4 chapters · 100%</p></div>
        <h1>Build systems that build systems.</h1>
        <p class="hero__dek">A dense, teaching-first companion to IndyDevDan’s course system. Each chapter turns the video spine into mental models, worked codebase examples, failure repairs, retrieval practice, and graded labs.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="progress-card" aria-label="Book progress">
        <p class="eyebrow">Corpus phase 1</p>
        <h2>18 of 18 chapters built</h2>
        <div class="progress-line" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
        <p class="progress-copy"><span>100% complete</span><span>Volume III · 4 of 4</span></p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <article class="chapter-feature">
      <div class="chapter-feature__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Now available · Volume III · Lesson 18</p>
        <h2>The Pi Verifier Agent</h2>
        <p class="chapter-feature__dek">Put an input-locked observer behind the builder, decompose every result into atomic claims, and spend extra compute to reclaim human review time.</p>
        <ul class="chapter-feature__meta"><li>Tactic · Spend Tokens to Save Time</li><li>60–90 min graded lab</li><li>12 full-width 4K frames</li><li>Build → verify → feedback → repeat</li></ul>
        <a class="button" href="vol-3-ma/18-verifier-agent.html">Start chapter →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="chapter-feature__map" aria-label="Verifier agent teaching arc">
        <div class="focus-three"><div>Builder · does the work</div><div>Verifier · checks atomic claims</div><div>Report · evidence and feedback</div></div>
      </div>
    </article>

